      "boundary": "Printed page 6 describes rectangular or logically rectangular grids and successive one-dimensional coordinate-direction problems. It does not define logical rectangularity through an explicit chart, topology, metric or Jacobian condition. The proposed interpretation uses coordinate connectivity, supplied physical cell volumes, shared normal face fluxes and successive conservative line updates, with actual measured Cartesian specialization. Whether this captures the intended logical geometry remains the pending source choice; solver totality/exactness is a separate representation issue addressed by the compiled admitted information-method sweep and arbitrary full-line Cartesian correspondence; neither result resolves the logical-geometry convention."
